.TH FATHOM_NARRATIVE 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-narrative \- Read one episode: the narrative every claim in it cites its evidence from (`e4.7`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom narrative\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-markdown\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-attribution\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIEPISODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read one episode: the narrative every claim in it cites its evidence from (`e4.7`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the claims, citations and weights as JSON on stdout, and nothing else there
.TP
\fB\-\-markdown\fR
Print the Markdown artefact body — the exact text `fathom export` will carry
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Print the ranking beside the prose: every claim\*(Aqs weight, so the order can be argued with
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<N>\fR
How many claims the *Read this first* paragraph holds (1 to 6)
.TP
\fB\-\-attribution\fR
Print whether a model wrote any of this, and the five gates a polish path must clear. Needs no index and no episode
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIEPISODE\fR]
The episode to read: an episode id, a commit, a rev (`HEAD~3`, `main`, `v1.2^{}`) or an oid prefix. Omitted with `\-\-attribution`, which answers a question about the build instead of an episode
